------Create Images and Deploy to Docker Desktop----
-run Docker Desktop
-Create Dockerfiles for Each Service
	user-service/Dockerfile
	order-service/Dockerfile
-build jar files of each mService:
	mvn clean package
-build Docker images:
	docker build -t user-service:latest .
	docker build -t order-service:latest .
-create a docker compose file:
	docker-compose.yml
-update service URL in the user-service service
String orderServiceUrl = "http://order-service:8082/orders/" + userId;
-start the services:
	docker-compose up
-check Docker Desktop
-test using
	http://localhost:8080/users/1/orders
	http://localhost:9090/orders/1

----Push images to Docker Hub-----
-docker login
-tag the images (tag will be latest)
docker tag user-service:latest jaberabbas/user-service:latest
docker tag order-service:latest jaberabbas/order-service:latest

-push images to Docker
docker push jaberabbas/user-service:latest
docker push jaberabbas/order-service:latest

------Deploy to kubernetes cluster----------

-create an AKS Azure cluster (in the US to have enough space)
-login to azure
	az login
-Set the context for kubectl to point to your AKS cluster:
	az aks get-credentials --resource-group <ResourceGroupName> --name <AKSClusterName>
-Create Kubernetes Deployment YAML Files:
	user-service/user-service-deployment.yaml
	order-service/order-service-deployment.yaml
-deploymentkubectl apply -f microservice1-deployment.yaml
	kubectl apply -f user-service-deployment.yaml
	kubectl apply -f order-deployment.yaml

-Verify the Deployment
	kubectl get deployments
	kubectl get pods
	kubectl get services

-Access to your mservices:
	C:\Users\j\workspace\Java\mservices\user-service>kubectl get services
	NAME            TYPE           CLUSTER-IP    EXTERNAL-IP      PORT(S)          AGE
	kubernetes      ClusterIP      10.0.0.1      <none>           443/TCP          21m
	order-service   LoadBalancer   10.0.144.93   172.179.61.236   9090:32488/TCP   6m34s
	user-service    LoadBalancer   10.0.182.22   172.179.62.93    8080:31764/TCP   86s
-Use the external IP to access your microservices:
http://172.179.62.93:8080/users/2/orders
http://172.179.61.236:9090/orders/1
-voilà, it works and it is done






